# Pinned SSH host keys for the fleet hosts in fleet/inventory.yml (OPS-33).
#
# Keyed by inventory host id, NOT by address: every fleet ssh call passes
# -o HostKeyAlias=<id> -o StrictHostKeyChecking=yes -o UserKnownHostsFile=<this file>
# (fleet/pinned-ssh.sh). Host keys are public data; the addresses stay in secrets.
# Never add `ssh-keyscan -H` lines here: a hashed IPv4 entry is brute-forceable back
# to the address, which this public repo promises not to carry.
#
# One ED25519 key per host. A key that does not match fails the SSH call loudly.
# Re-pin (reinstalled VPS, rotated host key): docs/RUNBOOK.md "Host key changed".
#
# SHA256 fingerprints, for eyeballing against `ssh-keygen -lf` on the host:
#   ovh-staging     SHA256:nEHWQurrW4s3cqbmkaHeoWy1Qmjgky5HTxA7jWyIYT4
#   ovh-devops-001  SHA256:TvZ3navXHLwyRRUPdjft/4JrW0haxQIoyP69UqXbdfg
#   hosting-vps     SHA256:xOHS/msE2NTLnTd1hMmmaJHjixMRWUPI/wbcr9WPkjw
